# screener

Source: https://api.unusualwhales.com/docs/openapi.yaml; retrieved 2026-09-24T01:21:27.462441+00:00

Full descriptions, inherited security, effective parameters, responses and schemas. No live calls.

## GET /api/option-activity/unusual

Unusual Options Activity

Returns option contracts flagged as unusual — the API equivalent of the [live options flow](https://unusualwhales.com/live-options-flow) "unusual" view.

This is the [Hottest Chains](https://api.unusualwhales.com/docs/operations/PublicApi.ScreenerController.contract_screener) screener with the `unusual` preset applied by default: the contract-expressible subset of the live-options-flow criteria — volume > OI, out-of-the-money, DTE ≤ 60, ask-side ≥ 50%, premium ≥ $10k, issue types ADR/Common Stock/ETF.

Every Hottest Chains filter is accepted here and overrides the preset (e.g. `?min_premium=25000&max_dte=30`); pass `unusual=false` to return the full screen. For the complete list of filters and the response shape see the [Hottest Chains endpoint](https://api.unusualwhales.com/docs/operations/PublicApi.ScreenerController.contract_screener).

For real time streaming of the same data, subscribe to the `contract_screener` websocket channel, see [https://api.unusualwhales.com/docs/operations/PublicApi.SocketController.contract_screener](https://api.unusualwhales.com/docs/operations/PublicApi.SocketController.contract_screener).

NOTE: Contracts with a volume of less than 200 are not being returned


